# Performance & Optimization

## Server Components (Performance First)

### Default to Server Components

**Server Components = Better Performance**:

```typescript
// ✅ Server Component (default) - Zero JavaScript to client
export default async function PropertiesPage() {
  const properties = await fetchProperties()
  return <PropertyList properties={properties} />
}
```

**Benefits**:
- Zero client-side JavaScript
- No hydration needed
- Faster initial load
- Better SEO
- Direct data access

### Client Components Only When Needed

```typescript
// ✅ Use Client Components sparingly
"use client"

import { useState } from 'react'

// Only interactive parts need to be Client Components
export function PropertyFilters({ onFilterChange }: Props) {
  const [filter, setFilter] = useState('')

  return (
    <select onChange={(e) => onFilterChange(e.target.value)}>
      {/* Options */}
    </select>
  )
}
```

## Data Fetching Optimization

### Parallel Data Fetching

```typescript
// ✅ Fetch in parallel
export default async function Dashboard() {
  const [properties, contracts, invoices] = await Promise.all([
    fetchProperties(),
    fetchContracts(),
    fetchInvoices()
  ])

  return (
    <>
      <PropertyList properties={properties} />
      <ContractList contracts={contracts} />
      <InvoiceList invoices={invoices} />
    </>
  )
}
```

### Sequential Fetching (When Dependencies Exist)

```typescript
// ✅ Sequential when one depends on another
export default async function PropertyPage({ params }: { params: { id: string } }) {
  const property = await fetchProperty(params.id)
  const owner = await fetchUser(property.OwnerCode) // Depends on property

  return <PropertyDetails property={property} owner={owner} />
}
```

### Caching Strategy

```typescript
// Static data (rarely changes)
const response = await fetch(url, {
  cache: 'force-cache' // Cache indefinitely
})

// Dynamic data (changes frequently)
const response = await fetch(url, {
  cache: 'no-store' // Never cache
})

// Revalidate periodically
const response = await fetch(url, {
  next: { revalidate: 3600 } // Revalidate every hour
})
```

## Image Optimization

### Next.js Image Component

```typescript
import Image from 'next/image'

// ✅ Always use Next.js Image
<Image
  src={property.CoverUrl}
  alt={property.Title}
  width={800}
  height={600}
  quality={80} // 1-100, default 75
  priority={false} // Set true for above-fold images
  placeholder="blur" // Blur placeholder while loading
  sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1200px) 50vw, 33vw"
/>
```

### Priority Loading

```typescript
// ✅ Above-fold images (visible without scrolling)
<Image
  src={hero.image}
  alt="Hero"
  priority={true} // Preload this image
  width={1920}
  height={1080}
/>

// ✅ Below-fold images (lazy load)
<Image
  src={property.image}
  alt="Property"
  priority={false} // Lazy load
  loading="lazy"
  width={400}
  height={300}
/>
```

### Responsive Images

```typescript
<Image
  src={property.CoverUrl}
  alt={property.Title}
  width={800}
  height={600}
  sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1200px) 50vw, 800px"
  // Generates optimized images for each breakpoint
/>
```

## Code Splitting

### Dynamic Imports

```typescript
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'

// ✅ Lazy load heavy components
const PropertyMap = dynamic(() => import('@/components/PropertyMap'), {
  ssr: false, // Don't render on server
  loading: () => <p>Loading map...</p>
})

// ✅ Lazy load chart libraries
const ApexChart = dynamic(() => import('react-apexcharts'), {
  ssr: false
})

export function PropertyDetails({ property }: Props) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>{property.Title}</h1>
      <PropertyMap coordinates={property.coordinates} />
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Route-based Code Splitting

Next.js automatically code-splits by route - no action needed.

## Bundle Size Optimization

### Import Only What You Need

```typescript
// ❌ Bad - imports entire library
import _ from 'lodash'

// ✅ Good - imports only needed function
import debounce from 'lodash/debounce'

// ❌ Bad - imports all icons
import * as Icons from 'lucide-react'

// ✅ Good - imports specific icons
import { Home, User, Settings } from 'lucide-react'
```

### Tree Shaking

```typescript
// ✅ Use named exports for better tree shaking
export function calculateTotal(items: Item[]) { }
export function formatPrice(price: number) { }

// Import only what you need
import { calculateTotal } from '@/lib/utils'
```

